Emergency Preparedness Operations Monthly Crime Log Commend Officer Student Break Parking Form Campus Crime Alerts Campus Hazing Act Lost and Found Items Traffic and Parking Regulations Evacuation Maps Career Services For Students For Employers Job Shadow: Employers Job Shadow: Employer Form Job Shadow: Employers FAQ For Alumni Church Relations Conference and Event Services Accommodations Inquiry Form Plan an Event FAQs Counseling Center Disability Services Students Parents Resources Family Engagement First-Generation Students Health Center Human Resources Employee Benefits VU Careers Living Well Community Resource Center Lyceum Theater Box Office Reporting Hotline Title IX Veteran Services Veteran Services How to Apply Military Education FAQ (opens in new window/tab) Veteran Resource Center VA Benefits Active-Duty Benefits Student Veteran Club Reserve Officer Training nav-breadcrumb Home > Resources > Career Services > For Students For Students Our Services Career Services provides complimentary services to current Vanguard University students and alumni. Our aim is that every student entering would utilize the career planning tools we have available to maximize their preparation prior to graduation. Here's an overview of our services: Career Advising VUConnect: Explore Jobs, Internships & More Career Advising Career Services offers free one-on-one individualized career advising to current Vanguard University students from undergraduate, graduate and professional studies programs, and all Lion alumni. Wherever you are in the career development process, we will be by your side. We invite you to schedule an appointment to develop a personalized plan. Appointment Topics Offered: Resume Review Cover Letter Review Mock Interview Job and Internship Search Graduate School Applications Assessment Results Career Direction and Planning Choosing a Major Personal Statement Review LinkedIn Profile Review VUConnect: Explore Jobs, Internships & More VUConnect is available to all Vanguard students for exploration of internships, jobs, and volunteer opportunities. Once enrolled in courses, students will be able to access this platform to find positions as well as engage with career development tools including a robust resume builder, mock interview system, and career guides. VUConnect is also our hub for all Career Services events, fairs, and scheduling appointments with a Career Advisor. Resources, Guides, and Handouts Federal Work Study and On Campus Student Jobs PATHWAYS DOCUMENTS Assessments Resumes Cover Letter Interviewing Networking What Can I Do With This Major? Career Direction Graduate School Federal Work Study and On Campus Student Jobs HOW DOES FEDERAL WORK STUDY (FWS) WORK? FWS provides employment and community service opportunities for students who are eligible for need-based financial aid. Awards are made based on the availability of funding and the student’s financial need, as determined by the FAFSA, and are communicated through VU's Financial Aid Office. Students who are awarded FWS are not guaranteed employment. Though these funds are intended to assist with paying educational costs, FWS funds are not considered in the college payment plan, as they are paid directly to students via a paycheck that is issued twice monthly as the student works. Current FWS / on campus employment opportunities can be found in VUConnect. Students not eligible for FWS may still apply for on campus jobs paid by Vanguard University. PATHWAYS DOCUMENTS Assessments Learning about your personality type, career interests, work values, skills, and strengths will help you make better-informed career choices. Career Services offers various assessments with individualized interpretation and counseling. Focus 2 Assessment Instructions Once you’ve taken these assessments, schedule an appointment with Career Services. We’ll go over your results and help you discover how your assessment results play into a potential career! Resumes Resume Guidelines and Samples Resume Template Resume Review Check List Identifying Your Accomplishments Transferable Skills Cover Letter Cover Letter Guidelines and Samples Cover Letter Template Interviewing Interviewing Guide Elevator Speech Behavioral Interviewing Networking Elevator Speech Networking Tracking Tool Network For Your Job Search Informational Interview What Can I Do With This Major? The What Can I Do With This Major? resource offers an overview of academic majors along with examples of career fields, industries, and tips, and links to help you research future opportunities. Career Direction Career Development Process Developing Career Goals Holistically Choosing A Career Reflecting Who You Are Informational Review Graduate School To Go or Not to Go Personal Statement Letter of Recommendation Graduate School Timeline Curriculum Vitae (CV) Editable Layout Upcoming Events September 10, 2026 10 a.m.–1 p.m. October 20, 2026 10 a.m.–1 p.m. February 9, 2027 10 a.m.–1 p.m. Various dates by academic degree APPLY NOW For Students For Employers For Alumni Contact us: Scott 242 careerservices@vanguard.edu 714-619-6474 Signs of fraudulent employers Follow Us footer-container-main Vanguard University A top private Christian university in Orange County, California 55 Fair Drive, Costa Mesa , CA 92626 Map & Directions Contact Us Facebook (opens in new window/tab) Instagram (opens in new window/tab) YouTube (opens in new window/tab) LinkedIn (opens in new window/tab) Schools & Centers College of Arts & Sciences Patty Arvielo School of Business & Management School of Education School of Theology & Ministry Global Center for Women & Justice (opens in new window/tab) Jesse Miranda Center for Hispanic Leadership Judkins Institute for Leadership Studies Lewis Wilson Institute for Pentecostal Studies Resources Job Openings Campus Safety Library Bookstore Registrar Events Press Room News Reporting Legal Notices Text Messaging Terms of Service Title IX Privacy Policy Reporting & Compliance Memberships