 Emergency Preparedness Operations Monthly Crime Log Commend Officer Student Break Parking Form Campus Crime Alerts Campus Hazing Act Lost and Found Items Traffic and Parking Regulations Evacuation Maps Career Services For Students For Employers Job Shadow: Employers Job Shadow: Employer Form Job Shadow: Employers FAQ For Alumni Church Relations Conference and Event Services Accommodations Inquiry Form Plan an Event FAQs Counseling Center Disability Services Students Parents Resources Family Engagement First-Generation Students Health Center Human Resources Employee Benefits VU Careers Living Well Community Resource Center Lyceum Theater Box Office Reporting Hotline Title IX Veteran Services Veteran Services How to Apply Military Education FAQ (opens in new window/tab) Veteran Resource Center VA Benefits Active-Duty Benefits Student Veteran Club Reserve Officer Training nav-breadcrumb Home > Resources > Career Services > For Employers For Employers Recruit From Vanguard What makes a Vanguard student different? Their character. Our students not only attend class with excellent academic content, they are mentored by professors and staff across campus. A Vanguard student is taught what it means to live life with integrity. This makes our students stand out in the workplace. Fairs Post A Job or Internship Opportunity On Campus Recruiting Job Shadow Program Company Visits & Informational Interviews Why Offer Internships? Campus Map GUIDELINES Fairs Registration for our fairs now occurs on our new platform VUConnect, powered by Symplicity. Please create an Employer account to begin the registration process. Once your account is approved, you will  find all of our available event registrations on your profile. Then, you can register for the ones that fit your organization's needs. September 10, 2026, from 10 a.m.–1 p.m. October 20, 2026, from 10 a.m.–1 p.m. Various dates by academic disciplines Find exact dates on VUConnect February 9, 2026, from 10 a.m.–1 p.m. Post A Job or Internship Opportunity Vanguard utilizes VUConnect , a modern college recruiting platform to provide you with a one-stop-shop to meet your recruiting needs for all paid jobs and internships. Sign Up on VUConnect Please note: Beginning May 1, 2024, all postings will be on VUConnect. Handshake will no longer be accessible to VU students or employers as of June 30, 2024. On Campus Recruiting Host a recruitment table on campus to connect with students, increase your visibility by sharing company information, and support your recruiting efforts. On-campus recruiting is a great way to engage students for jobs, internships and volunteer opportunities. In order to be approved for on-campus recruiting, please fill out the form by clicking on the below link. We have a committee that will review your information and will get back to you as to the status of your request. On-Campus Recruiting Application On-campus recruiting requests must be submitted 30 days prior to your recruiting date. Vanguard University gives priority to groups that have partnered with Vanguard in the past through one of Career Services’ annual resource fairs. PLEASE NOTE if you do not show up on your scheduled date for on campus recruiting without prior notification, per our policy, you will have to re-apply in the following semester. Job Shadow Program We believe that one of the best ways for students to succeed is to explore and experience opportunities first hand. Our Job Shadow Program allows current students to meet with current professionals to explore opportunities in a given industry while giving the employer access to potential candidates for internship and job openings. Learn More Company Visits & Informational Interviews Our students are encouraged both in and out of the classroom to engage in their desired vocation field throughout their academic career. Two of these avenues are through: Company visits in which faculty bring students to tour and learning from those in industry-specific companies, and Informational interviews in which students meet with a professional in their desired field to learn more about the vocation, additional schooling, and steps to take towards the profession. If you or your company is interested, please contact careerservices@vanguard.edu Why Offer Internships? By offering internships to Vanguard University students, you are helping train and develop the next generation of professionals. Paid internships are an excellent addition to your organization, as they give you the chance to: Find potential future employees who are motivated to succeed Gain new perspectives from a diverse student demographic Complete important projects more efficiently Enhance the visibility of your organization on campus and in the community Campus Map Participating in a fair or student recruitment event? Here is our Campus Map . GUIDELINES By participating in on-campus recruiting or posting a job/internship on Handshake, employers agree to follow the policies set forth below. General Employer Guidelines NACE Vanguard University Career Services is a member of the National Association of Colleges and Employers (NACE) and adheres to guidelines set forth in the NACE Principles for Professional Practice. We expect employers who recruit at Vanguard University to adhere to the Principles for Employment Professionals. Equal Employment Opportunity Employers must adhere to the Equal Employment Opportunity Commission (EEOC) recruitment and employment laws and the Department of Labor. Right to Refuse Service We reserve the right to refuse service to employers for factors such as: Misrepresentation by dishonesty or lack of information Fraud Complaints by students Requiring, at the time of application, personal information such as bank and social security numbers Personal funding required to obtain the position Failure to adhere to local, state and federal laws Promoting specific products rather than promoting a job or internship Unpaid Internships Organizations are asked to review the Guidelines from the Department of Labor. For Students For Employers For Alumni Upcoming Events There are no events to display Contact Us Scott Academic Center, 2nd floor Careerservices@vanguard.edu 714.619.6474 footer-container-main Vanguard University A top private Christian university in Orange County, California 55 Fair Drive, Costa Mesa , CA 92626 Map & Directions Contact Us Facebook (opens in new window/tab) Instagram (opens in new window/tab) YouTube (opens in new window/tab) LinkedIn (opens in new window/tab) Schools & Centers College of Arts & Sciences Patty Arvielo School of Business & Management School of Education School of Theology & Ministry Global Center for Women & Justice (opens in new window/tab) Jesse Miranda Center for Hispanic Leadership Judkins Institute for Leadership Studies Lewis Wilson Institute for Pentecostal Studies Resources Job Openings Campus Safety Library Bookstore Registrar Events Press Room News Reporting Legal Notices Text Messaging Terms of Service Title IX Privacy Policy Reporting & Compliance Memberships & Affiliations footer-wrapper utilities Costa Mesa, CA Resources Site Map footer-tracking remarketing <div style=\"display:inline;\"> \n<img height=\"1\" width=\"1\" style=\"border-style:none;\" alt=\"\" src=\"//googleads.g.doubleclick.net/pagead/viewthroughconversion/1033647084/?value=0&amp;guid=ON&amp;script=0\"/> \n</div> footer-tracking sharpspring Powered by Finalsite"
