ublic Safety Emergency Preparedness Operations Monthly Crime Log Commend Officer Student Break Parking Form Campus Crime Alerts Campus Hazing Act Lost and Found Items Traffic and Parking Regulations Evacuation Maps Career Services For Students For Employers Job Shadow: Employers Job Shadow: Employer Form Job Shadow: Employers FAQ For Alumni Church Relations Conference and Event Services Accommodations Inquiry Form Plan an Event FAQs Counseling Center Disability Services Students Parents Resources Family Engagement First-Generation Students Health Center Human Resources Employee Benefits VU Careers Living Well Community Resource Center Lyceum Theater Box Office Reporting Hotline Title IX Veteran Services Veteran Services How to Apply Military Education FAQ (opens in new window/tab) Veteran Resource Center VA Benefits Active-Duty Benefits Student Veteran Club Reserve Officer Training nav-breadcrumb Home > Resources > Career Services > For Employers > Job Shadow: Employers > Job Shadow: Employers FAQ Job Shadow: Employers FAQ About the Job Shadow Program The Job Shadow Program is a one-day, experiential learning opportunity that exposes students to potential career paths and work environments. The program introduces students to professional work culture, as well as career opportunities that relate to their interests and skills. Employers may choose to host students virtually or in-person. Frequently Asked Questions Important Dates Can I host a student virtually? Can I participate for a full or partial day? Can I host more than one student for the program? What will the student be doing while they are at my company? Does Vanguard decide that or do we? When will I host a student with my company? How will the student get to my company? Are we responsible for transportation? How are students selected to participate in this program? How are they matched with my company? When is the submission time frame for participating in the Job Shadow Program? What are the benefits for participating? Important Dates Can I host a student virtually? Yes. Please indicate on your Employer Form whether you will be hosting a student in person or virtually. Here are a few ideas for a virtual scenario: Allow a student join a zoom meeting that involves multiple team members and then discuss it with student afterwards Provide student with a verbal overview of what employer does and allow her/him to ask questions Do a “share screen” with student while working on a particular project Allow student to sit in on a phone call or presentation with a client Can I participate for a full or partial day? You may choose to host a student for either a full day (6-8 hours), a partial day (4 hours) or a multi-day (2 days). Simply indicate what you prefer on the Employer form . Can I host more than one student for the program? Yes! You may choose to host one or more students for the Job Shadow Program. If hosting more than one student, you may choose to host the students at various departments at your company. You can indicate how many students you prefer to host on the Employer form . What will the student be doing while they are at my company? Does Vanguard decide that or do we? The employer partner is responsible for creating a schedule for the job shadow day. The schedule could consist of a tour of the organization, observing certain work functions, attending engaging meetings, participating in events, a networking lunch with staff, conducting informational interviews, formal opportunities for students to ask questions, etc. SAMPLE AGENDA 9:00 AM – 10:00 AM Arrival, Introductions to Staff 10:00 AM – 10:30 AM Presentation/Company Overview from Executive 10:30 AM – 11:00 AM Tour of Facility 11:00 AM – 12:00 PM Observe Work 12:00 PM – 1:00 PM Lunch with Staff 1:00 PM – 2:00 PM Observe Work 2:00 PM – 3:00 PM Hands-on Activity 3:00 PM – 4:00 PM Wrap up / Questions / Reflections When will I host a student with my company? The Job Shadow Program takes place between February 14, 2025 - April 25, 2025, for the Spring. The Summer program dates are from May 15 to August 15, and the Fall program dates are from October 15 to December 15. It is up to the employer to have established date(s) or schedule directly with the student upon being paired. How will the student get to my company? Are we responsible for transportation? If your opportunity is in-person, students are responsible for providing their own transportation to and from the employer. How are students selected to participate in this program? How are they matched with my company? Students interested in participating in the Job Shadow Program will be required to fill out an application through the Career Services office at Vanguard University. The team will select the student(s) who will participate in the shadow day at your organization, based on the student’s major, career interests, and spring break location preferences. Once your student has been selected, we will provide you with information about their background prior to the scheduled shadow date. Note: We cannot guarantee that every employer will be matched with a student. We will match as many students with employers as possible. When is the submission time frame for participating in the Job Shadow Program? We do have an ongoing recruitment window, however the submission timeframe is as follows: Spring: January 15, 2025 Summer: March 15, 2025 Fall: September 30, 2025 What are the benefits for participating? Support a program that gives Vanguard students a competitive advantage Develop your employees’ mentoring, coaching and leadership skills Provides early identification of potential candidates for internships and full-time positions Showcase the daily activities, challenges and requirements of your organization Promote your organization to a younger network, introducing students to your culture Gain perspective and insight from the next generation Participate in a unique program that will allow you to promote your organization's social responsibility Questions? Interested in participating? Please contact the Career Services team at careerservices@vanguard.edu or 714-619-6474. For Students For Employers For Alumni Upcoming Events There are no events to display Contact Us Scott Academic Center, 2nd floor Careerservices@vanguard.edu 714.619.6474 footer-container-main Vanguard University A top private Christian university in Orange County, California 55 Fair Drive, Costa Mesa , CA 92626 Map & Directions Contact Us Facebook (opens in new window/tab) Instagram (opens in new window/tab) YouTube (opens in new window/tab) LinkedIn (opens in new window/tab) Schools & Centers College of Arts & Sciences Patty Arvielo School of Business & Management School of Education School of Theology & Ministry Global Center for Women & Justice (opens in new window/tab) Jesse Miranda Center for Hispanic Leadership Judkins Institute for Leadership Studies Lewis Wilson Institute for Pentecostal Studies Resources Job Openings Campus Safety Library Bookstore Registrar Events Press Room News Reporting Legal Notices Text Messaging Terms of Service Title IX Privacy Policy Reporting & Compliance Memberships & Affiliations footer-wrapper utilities Costa Mesa, CA Resources Site Map footer-tracking remarketing <div style=\"display:inline;\"> \n<img height=\"1\" width=\"1\" style=\"border-style:none;\" alt=\"\" src=\"//googleads.g.doubleclick.net/pagead/viewthroughconversion/1033647084/?value=0&amp;guid=ON&amp;script=0\"/> \n</div> footer-tracking sharpspring Powered by Finalsite"
