    "https://recruiting.myapps.paychex.com/appone/MainInfoReq.asp?R_ID=7048158": {
      "title": "Faculty and Chair Position",
      "description": "Job Information: Faculty and Chair Position - BSN Program Job Share Apply Now Title Faculty and Chair Position - BSN Program Description Position Summary: Vanguard University is looking for an outstanding nurse-educator would relish leading our Bachelor of Science in Nursing program, a role which includes teaching and mentoring in a warm and diverse community of people who are serious about following Jesus Christ. The BSN Program Chair is a full-time faculty member who teaches Medical-Surgical Nursing and provides day-to-day operational leadership for our BSN pre-licensure program. The Chair supports high-quality instruction, student progression and success, faculty coordination, and operational excellence. The role ensures ongoing compliance with regulatory and accreditation standards and advances Vanguard’s mission through academic excellence, service, and Christian commitment. Essential Functions: BSN Program Operational Leadership Provide daily coordination of BSN program operations, ensuring consistent execution of program policies, schedules, and processes. Oversee course scheduling, clinical and lab coordination (in collaboration with clinical placement coordinator), faculty teaching assignments, and coverage plans. Maintain program readiness for regulatory and accreditation expectations by supporting documentation, compliance tracking, and continuous quality improvement. Coordinate student progression processes (e.g., progression checkpoints, remediation pathways, retention supports) in alignment with program policies. Monitor key student outcomes and help implement improvement plans. Serve as a primary point of contact for day-to-day student issues requiring program-level coordination; escalate complex matters to the Director as appropriate. Support admissions, orientation, and student communication workflows in collaboration with Admissions and Student Services. Reports to the Director of Nursing Faculty and Course Coordination Lead BSN faculty operational coordination (e.g., course lead meetings, exam/assessment coordination, clinical evaluation consistency). Promote consistency across sections in course delivery, grading practices, clinical evaluation tools, and student communication. Support onboarding and mentoring of new and adjunct faculty; coordinate peer support, teaching resources, and compliance training. Curriculum and Assessment Support Support implementation of the BSN curriculum, including alignment of course objectives, learning activities, clinical experiences, and program outcomes. Participate in curriculum review and revision processes, including mapping to professional standards and Essentials/QSEN as used by the program. Teaching Responsibilities (Medical-Surgical Nursing) Teach assigned undergraduate Medical-Surgical Nursing didactic and/or clinical/lab sections, as determined by program need. Develop and deliver instruction using evidence-based teaching strategies and active learning methodologies. Contribute to simulation and skills development activities when assigned, collaborating with the Simulation Coordinator. Minimum Qualifications: Master’s degree in Nursing (MSN) from an accredited institution (or higher). Active, unencumbered California RN license (or eligibility to obtain). Minimum of two (2) years of recent clinical experience in medical-surgical nursing (or closely related adult health area). Prior teaching experience in nursing education (academic or staff development), with demonstrated effectiveness. Demonstrated organizational and leadership skills, including ability to coordinate complex schedules and operational workflows. Strong communication, collaboration, and conflict-resolution skills. Commitment to student success and the mission and values of Vanguard University. Preferred Qualifications: Doctoral degree (DNP, PhD, EdD) in Nursing or related field. Prior experience in program leadership (course lead, program coordinator, chair/coordinator, assistant director). Experience with simulation-based education and clinical evaluation frameworks. SALARY Full-time position. Rank and salary are commensurate with qualifications and experience. Highly qualified candidates may be considered for an appointment to an endowed professorship with additional compensation. Assistant Professor: $60,595 to $81,501 Associate Professor: $70,676 to $95,190 Professor: $82,031 to $113,974 Placement at appropriate rank (e.g., Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor) and initial salary is dependent upon education, experience, and based on Vanguard’s faculty compensation schedule. The upper range is reserved for candidates that demonstrate the highest level of proficiency within a particular rank. Vanguard University also offers a very competitive and generous benefits package. Vanguard offers both tenure track and term faculty contracts; the type of contract offered will be determined based on the candidate’s qualifications at the time of hire. In recognition of the current market demand for nursing faculty, a discipline-based market adjustment may be applied to the base salary. Questions about this position may be directed to Human Resources at hr@vanguard.edu. APPLICATION PROCEDURE Please complete the application and upload the required documents below. Please do not send your documents directly to the Department Chair. Accompanying Essays: Personal Testimony of Relationship with Jesus Christ. Please provide a brief account of your experience of coming to faith in Christ. Include current church attendance, ministry, outreach and service involvement, any experience you have had with the Assemblies of God or other Pentecostal churches. Philosophy of Christian Education and Role of a Christian University. Explain what you believe to be the elements essential to the educational theory & practice of a Christian University. Integration of Faith, Teaching and Scholarship. Explain how you integrate your faith with your discipline & in your teaching and scholarship. Curriculum vitae includes: Colleges/universities attended, location, & degree or units earned. Majors or fields of study, undergrad & graduate majors, minors, & areas of concentration. With the most recent, a chronological listing of teaching experience - name and location of institutions, title/academic rank, full/part-time, dates of employment A specific listing of courses previously taught Publications, presentations, honors, awards, and memberships in professional organizations With the most recent employment, position/title, full/part-time, dates of employment Any other qualifying experience, paid/voluntary, other. References - Names, e-mail, and phone numbers of at least 3 people not related to you whom we may contact for an evaluation of your professional abilities. Pastoral reference letter - Pastor or church leader. Transcripts - Unofficial transcripts accepted to apply. If selected, notarized transcripts are required prior to employment. * All of the above requested attachments must be included with your application in order to be considered. Applications will be accepted until position is filled or until there are a sufficient number of applicants. EOE Statement Vanguard University is committed to ensure that all candidates have an equitable opportunity to apply for and participate in the selection process. As a university, we hold firm to the application of the reasonable accommodation process in accordance with the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990. If you require an accommodation because of a disability in order to participate in any phase of the application process, or if you would like to request this information in an alternative format, please call Ken Bott, Sr. Director of Human Resources, at 714-662-5287. Vanguard University is an equal opportunity employer and prohibits discrimination or harassment of any kind against individuals of race, color, national origin, disability, pregnancy or any other characteristic outlined by federal, state, and local laws. Where permitted by law and in relation to the school's heritage and mission, Vanguard does exercise religious preference throughout the University and therefore employs individuals who are compatible with the institution, mission and statement of faith. This applies to all employment practices within the university. Vanguard is committed to a hiring process that is based on candidate's qualifications, merit, and operational needs of the university. Category Faculty Full-Time/Part-Time Full-Time Exempt/Non-Exempt Exempt This position is currently accepting applications. Apply Now App One .com TM ©1999-2024 HR Services, Inc. Click here for technical assistance. We use cookies and other technologies to support site functionality, analytics, preferences, marketing, and to improve your experience and our services.\r\n        We use third party technologies that may access your information. By continuing to use our site, you expressly consent to such use.\r\n        For more information, see our Privacy Policy. Continue We use cookies and other technologies to support site functionality, analytics, preferences, and to improve your experience and our services. We use third party technologies that may access your information.\r\n\t        By continuing to use our site, you expressly consent to such use. For more information, see our Privacy Policy. Continue"
    },
    "https://recruiting.myapps.paychex.com/appone/MainInfoReq.asp?R_ID=7195498": {
      "title": "Faculty Position",
      "description": "Job Information: Faculty Position - Business & Management  Job Share Apply Now Title Faculty Position - Business & Management Description POSITION SUMMARY The Department of Business and Management invites applications for a tenure-track or professional position in business and management at the Assistant or Associate Professor level, effective January 2026. Areas of specialization are open; however, preference will be given to candidates with the background to teach a variety of general topics across the disciplines of business and management, ranging from Introduction to Business to upper-division courses in Business Law, Negotiation and Conflict Management, Human Resources and Industrial/Organizational Psychology, and Social Entrepreneurship. A well-qualified business and management faculty member will be a critical thinker who combines insight, creativity, and technology with a practical approach to business and management education. This position may also include the opportunity to serve as chair of the Department of Business and Management, based on the candidate’s qualifications and institutional needs. The Department of Business and Management at Vanguard University is part of the Patty Arvielo School of Business and Management and currently offers a BA in Accounting, Business Administration, and Marketing. The department is home to COMPASS, a professional development co-curricular program, and a thriving student Accounting Society. The department fosters a collaborative, supportive environment for faculty with opportunities for personal growth and leadership. ABOUT VANGUARD UNIVERSITY AND THE PATTY ARVIELO SCHOOL OF BUSINESS AND MANAGEMENT Orange County's first four-year college, Vanguard has been equipping students since 1920 for a Spirit-empowered life of Christ-centered leadership and service. Today we continue to offer a top-rated Christian education, combined with practical skills and training in liberal arts, sciences and professional programs, to prepare students for the next chapter in their life. With a tight-knit community of 2,200 students, Vanguard is a campus where each student is known; where their story matters. The Patty Arvielo School of Business and Management at Vanguard University, launched in fall 2024, is the first U.S. business school named after a Latina. Honoring Patty Arvielo, co-founder of New American Funding, the school benefits from a significant donation that supports graduate program development, endowed faculty chairs, and scholarships. Patty Arvielo’s inspiring story as a first-generation Latina resonates with Vanguard’s diverse student body. Today, nearly half of our undergraduate students are Hispanic and Vanguard is a federally designated Hispanic Serving Institution. A strong commitment to cultural diversity, racial reconciliation, and gender equality is a consequence of Vanguard being deeply grounded in the faith tradition that brought the University into existence. Moreover, these core values continue to define the institutional vision that pulls the Vanguard community forward toward its mission and educational targets and goals. Within this Christian context of inclusiveness, the University aims to provide a quality educational experience by promoting academic excellence that integrates faith and life and providing professor-mentors in a dynamic community environment. Vanguard is located in beautiful Orange County, CA and enjoys easy proximity to Southern California beaches, Disneyland and numerous Fortune 500 and 1000 companies. POSITION DUTIES Teach undergraduate and graduate coursework in a wide range of business and management courses. Faculty teach on a 4/4 schedule (24 units/academic year) as well as on-campus and online as needs are identified. Transfer knowledge including theory, practical skills, methods and techniques in his/her related field. Challenge thinking, foster debate and develop the ability of students to engage in critical discourse and thinking. Participate in general faculty roles in areas including advising and committee service. Participate in the building of an innovative Christian university. Take part in department and university decision-making and shared governance. Exercise academic leadership in the design and development of curricula. Collaborate with department faculty in curriculum implementation, student support, and continuous program improvement. Assist with development of new initiatives and delivery systems. Assist with facilitation of continuing accreditation through participation in professional development opportunities and in the preparation of program review documents and assessment processes. Assist in building relationships with Orange County businesses and employers; assist with continuous strengthening of program links to and service to the community. Participate in mentoring students by advising, responding to questions appropriate for student/faculty interactions, and meeting with students as needed or requested. The department chair position includes the following functions, which can be specified upon request: Recruiting and supervising departmental personnel. Continuously assessing educational effectiveness of departmental programs. Strategic planning and budget management for the department. Attending to student needs. Promoting the department throughout the University and to external publics. Managing needs for effective operation of the department. QUALIFICATIONS Candidates with a PhD/DBA/JD are preferred. Qualified individuals with an MBA plus a combination of extensive teaching and business experience will be considered. Relevant industry certifications would be an added advantage. Evidence of teaching effectiveness in a variety of undergraduate and graduate courses in business and management, ranging from Introduction to Business to upper-division courses in Business Law, Negotiation and Conflict Management, Human Resources and Industrial/Organizational Psychology, and Social Entrepreneurship. Candidates must have evidence of a strong commitment to teaching in a liberal arts environment. Interacting with students, working collaboratively with faculty from other disciplines, faculty and leadership with different backgrounds and points of view and a deep appreciation of and respect for academic values, and culture must be a top priority of the candidate. Demonstrated teaching ability at the undergraduate level. Experience with hyflex and/or online delivery methods preferred. Proficiency or strong familiarity with the Microsoft Office suite of applications and the Canvas learning management system or equivalent LMS. A vibrant Christian faith and commitment to an integration of faith and learning. For the department chair, candidates should provide evidence of administrative experience in higher education. SALARY This is a full-time position. Placement at the appropriate faculty rank and salary are based on qualifications, education, experience, and Vanguard University's faculty compensation schedule. Assistant Professor: $60,595 to $81,501 Associate Professor: $70,676 to $95,190 Highly qualified candidates may be considered for appointment as Department Chair, with additional compensation. Vanguard University also offers a very generous benefits package . Vanguard offers both tenure-track and term faculty contracts. The type of contract offered will be determined based on the candidate's qualifications at the time of hire. APPLICATION PROCEDURE To apply, please complete the online application and upload the required documents listed below. Please do not send application materials directly to the Department Chair. As you begin the application process, please be prepared to submit the following documents. If you experience any technical difficulties or have questions regarding the application process, please contact the Office of Human Resources at hr@vanguard.edu for assistance. Required Essays Personal Testimony of Relationship with Jesus Christ. Please provide a brief account of your experience of coming to faith in Christ. Include current church attendance, ministry, outreach and service involvement, any experience you have had with the Assemblies of God or other Pentecostal churches. Philosophy of Christian Education and Role of a Christian University. Explain what you believe to be the elements essential to the educational theory & practice of a Christian University. Integration of Faith, Teaching and Scholarship. Explain how you integrate your faith with your discipline & in your teaching and scholarship. Curriculum Vitae (CV) - CV should include: Colleges/universities attended, location, & degree or units earned. Majors or fields of study, undergrad & graduate majors, minors, & areas of concentration. With the most recent, a chronological listing of teaching experience - name and location of institutions, title/academic rank, full/part-time, dates of employment A specific listing of courses previously taught Publications, presentations, honors, awards, and memberships in professional organizations With the most recent employment, position/title, full/part-time, dates of employment Any other qualifying experience, paid/voluntary, other. References - Please provide the names, email addresses, and phone numbers of at least three professional references who are not related to you and who can speak to your professional qualifications. Pastoral Reference letter - Submit a reference letter from your pastor or another church leader. Transcripts - Unofficial transcripts are acceptable for the application process. If selected for employment, official (or otherwise required verified) transcripts must be submitted prior to employment. EOE Statement Vanguard University is committed to ensure that all candidates have an equitable opportunity to apply for and participate in the selection process. As a university, we hold firm to the application of the reasonable accommodation process in accordance with the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990. If you require an accommodation because of a disability in order to participate in any phase of the application process, or if you would like to request this information in an alternative format, please call Ken Bott, Sr. Director of Human Resources, at 714-662-5287. Vanguard University is an equal opportunity employer and prohibits discrimination or harassment of any kind against individuals of race, color, national origin, disability, pregnancy or any other characteristic outlined by federal, state, and local laws. Where permitted by law and in relation to the school's heritage and mission, Vanguard does exercise religious preference throughout the University and therefore employs individuals who are compatible with the institution, mission and statement of faith. This applies to all employment practices within the university. Vanguard is committed to a hiring process that is based on candidate's qualifications, merit, and operational needs of the university. Category School of Business and Management Full-Time/Part-Time Full-Time Exempt/Non-Exempt Exempt This position is currently accepting applications. Apply Now App One .com TM ©1999-2024 HR Services, Inc. Click here for technical assistance. We use cookies and other technologies to support site functionality, analytics, preferences, marketing, and to improve your experience and our services.\r\n        We use third party technologies that may access your information. By continuing to use our site, you expressly consent to such use.\r\n        For more information, see our Privacy Policy. Continue We use cookies and other technologies to support site functionality, analytics, preferences, and to improve your experience and our services. We use third party technologies that may access your information.\r\n\t        By continuing to use our site, you expressly consent to such use. For more information, see our Privacy Policy. Continue"
    },
    "https://recruiting.myapps.paychex.com/appone/MainInfoReq.asp?R_ID=6597588": {
      "title": "Faculty Position",
      "description": "Job Information: Faculty Position - Finance Job Share Apply Now Title Faculty Position - Finance Description POSITION SUMMARY The Department of Business and Management invites applications for tenure track or a professional position in finance at the Assistant or Associate Professor level, effective January 2027. Areas of specialization are open; however, preference will be given to candidates with expertise in Real Estate, Entrepreneurial & Venture Capital, Corporate Finance, and Banking & Institutions. A well-qualified finance faculty will be a critical thinker who combines insight, creativity, and technology with a practical approach to finance education. The Department of Business and Management at Vanguard University is part of the Patty Arvielo School of Business and Management and currently offers a BA in Accounting, Business Administration, and Marketing. The department is home to COMPASS, a professional development co-curricular program, and a thriving student Accounting Society. The department fosters a collaborative, supportive environment for faculty with opportunities for personal growth and leadership. ABOUT VANGUARD UNIVERSITY AND THE PATTY ARVIELO SCHOOL OF BUSINESS AND MANAGEMENT Orange County's first four-year college, Vanguard has been equipping students since 1920 for a Spirit-empowered life of Christ-centered leadership and service. Today we continue to offer a top-rated Christian education, combined with practical skills and training in liberal arts, sciences and professional programs, to prepare students for the next chapter in their life. With a tight-knit community of 2,200 students, Vanguard is a campus where each student is known; where their story matters. The Patty Arvielo School of Business and Management at Vanguard University, launched in fall 2024, is the first U.S. business school named after a Latina. Honoring Patty Arvielo, co-founder of New American Funding, the school benefits from a significant donation that supports graduate program development, endowed faculty chairs, and scholarships. Patty Arvielo’s inspiring story as a first-generation Latina resonates with Vanguard’s diverse student body. Today, nearly half of our undergraduate students are Hispanic and Vanguard is a federally designated Hispanic Serving Institution. A strong commitment to cultural diversity, racial reconciliation, and gender equality is a consequence of Vanguard being deeply grounded in the faith tradition that brought the University into existence. Moreover, these core values continue to define the institutional vision that pulls the Vanguard community forward toward its mission and educational targets and goals. Within this Christian context of inclusiveness, the University aims to provide a quality educational experience by promoting academic excellence that integrates faith and life and providing professor-mentors in a dynamic community environment. Vanguard is located in beautiful Orange County, CA and enjoys easy proximity to Southern California beaches, Disneyland and numerous Fortune 500 and 1000 companies. POSITION DUTIES Teach undergraduate and graduate coursework in finance, real estate and other business courses. Faculty teach on a 4/4 schedule (24 units/academic year) as well as in-person and online as needs are identified. Transfer knowledge including theory, practical skills, methods and techniques in his/her related field. Challenge thinking, foster debate and develop the ability of students to engage in critical discourse and thinking. Participate in general faculty roles in areas including advising and committee service. Participate in the building of an innovative Christian university. Take part in department and university decision-making and governance. Exercise academic leadership in the design and development of curricula. Collaborate with department faculty in curriculum implementation, student support, and continuous program improvement. Assist with development of new initiatives and delivery systems. Assist with facilitation of continuing accreditation through participation in professional development opportunities and in the preparation of program review documents and assessment processes. Assist in building relationships with Orange County businesses and employers; assist with continuous strengthening of program links to and service to the community. Participate in the mentoring of students through advising, responding to questions appropriate to student/faculty interaction, and meet with students as needed or requested. Identify risks to the organization within the department and discuss risk reduction options with immediate supervisor. QUALIFICATIONS Candidates with a PhD/DBA in Finance are preferred. Qualified individuals with an M.Sc./MBA in economics/finance plus a combination of extensive teaching and finance industry experience will be considered. Relevant industry certifications would be an added advantage Evidence of teaching effectiveness in a variety of undergraduate courses, including Corporate Finance, Real Estate Finance, Entrepreneurial Finance, Financial Strategy, Commercial Banking & Credit Analysis, and Capital Markets. Candidates must have evidence of a strong commitment to teaching in a liberal arts environment. Interacting with students, working collaboratively with faculty from other disciplines, faculty and leadership with different backgrounds and points of view and a deep appreciation of and respect for academic values, and culture must be a top priority of the candidate. Demonstrated teaching ability at the undergraduate level. Experience with hyflex and/or online delivery methods preferred. Proficiency or strong familiarity with the Microsoft Office suite of applications and the Canvas learning management system or equivalent LMS. A vibrant Christian faith, and commitment to an integration of faith and learning.???? SALARY This is a full-time position. Placement at the appropriate faculty rank and salary are based on qualifications, education, experience, and Vanguard University's faculty compensation schedule. Assistant Professor: $60,595 to $81,501 Associate Professor: $70,676 to $95,190 Highly qualified candidates may be considered for appointment as Department Chair, with additional compensation. Vanguard University also offers a very generous benefits package. Vanguard offers both tenure-track and term faculty contracts. The type of contract offered will be determined based on the candidate's qualifications at the time of hire. APPLICATION PROCEDURE To apply, please complete the online application and upload the required documents listed below. Please do not send application materials directly to the Department Chair. As you begin the application process, please be prepared to submit the following documents. If you experience any technical difficulties or have questions regarding the application process, please contact the Office of Human Resources at hr@vanguard.edu for assistance. Required Essays Personal Testimony of Relationship with Jesus Christ. Please provide a brief account of your experience of coming to faith in Christ. Include current church attendance, ministry, outreach and service involvement, any experience you have had with the Assemblies of God or other Pentecostal churches. Philosophy of Christian Education and Role of a Christian University. Explain what you believe to be the elements essential to the educational theory & practice of a Christian University. Integration of Faith, Teaching and Scholarship. Explain how you integrate your faith with your discipline & in your teaching and scholarship. Curriculum Vitae (CV) - CV should include: Colleges/universities attended, location, & degree or units earned. Majors or fields of study, undergrad & graduate majors, minors, & areas of concentration. With the most recent, a chronological listing of teaching experience - name and location of institutions, title/academic rank, full/part-time, dates of employment A specific listing of courses previously taught Publications, presentations, honors, awards, and memberships in professional organizations With the most recent employment, position/title, full/part-time, dates of employment Any other qualifying experience, paid/voluntary, other. References - Please provide the names, email addresses, and phone numbers of at least three professional references who are not related to you and who can speak to your professional qualifications. Pastoral Reference letter - Submit a reference letter from your pastor or another church leader. Transcripts - Unofficial transcripts are acceptable for the application process. If selected for employment, official (or otherwise required verified) transcripts must be submitted prior to employment. EOE Statement Vanguard University is committed to ensure that all candidates have an equitable opportunity to apply for and participate in the selection process. As a university, we hold firm to the application of the reasonable accommodation process in accordance with the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990. If you require an accommodation because of a disability in order to participate in any phase of the application process, or if you would like to request this information in an alternative format, please call Ken Bott, Sr. Director of Human Resources, at 714-662-5287. Vanguard University is an equal opportunity employer and prohibits discrimination or harassment of any kind against individuals of race, color, national origin, disability, pregnancy or any other characteristic outlined by federal, state, and local laws. Where permitted by law and in relation to the school's heritage and mission, Vanguard does exercise religious preference throughout the University and therefore employs individuals who are compatible with the institution, mission and statement of faith. This applies to all employment practices within the university. Vanguard is committed to a hiring process that is based on candidate's qualifications, merit, and operational needs of the university. Category Faculty Full-Time/Part-Time Full-Time Exempt/Non-Exempt Exempt This position is currently accepting applications. Apply Now App One .com TM ©1999-2024 HR Services, Inc. Click here for technical assistance. We use cookies and other technologies to support site functionality, analytics, preferences, marketing, and to improve your experience and our services.\r\n        We use third party technologies that may access your information. By continuing to use our site, you expressly consent to such use.\r\n        For more information, see our Privacy Policy. Continue We use cookies and other technologies to support site functionality, analytics, preferences, and to improve your experience and our services. We use third party technologies that may access your information.\r\n\t        By continuing to use our site, you expressly consent to such use. For more information, see our Privacy Policy. Continue"
