ty Emergency Preparedness Operations Monthly Crime Log Commend Officer Student Break Parking Form Campus Crime Alerts Campus Hazing Act Lost and Found Items Traffic and Parking Regulations Evacuation Maps Career Services For Students For Employers Job Shadow: Employers Job Shadow: Employer Form Job Shadow: Employers FAQ For Alumni Church Relations Conference and Event Services Accommodations Inquiry Form Plan an Event FAQs Counseling Center Disability Services Students Parents Resources Family Engagement First-Generation Students Health Center Human Resources Employee Benefits VU Careers Living Well Community Resource Center Lyceum Theater Box Office Reporting Hotline Title IX Veteran Services Veteran Services How to Apply Military Education FAQ (opens in new window/tab) Veteran Resource Center VA Benefits Active-Duty Benefits Student Veteran Club Reserve Officer Training nav-breadcrumb Home > Resources > Human Resources Human Resources At Vanguard University, work is more than a role—it’s a calling. At Vanguard University, work is more than a role—it’s a calling. Our Human Resources team fosters a Christ-centered community where you’re empowered to grow, lead, and make a meaningful impact. We support our employees through comprehensive benefits including health coverage, retirement, paid time off, and tuition remission. Explore job opportunities and discover where you are called to be. Your story matters here. Job Opportunities Explore Benefits Contact Us Hours: Mondays —Fridays, 8:00 a.m. —5:00 p.m. Email: hr@vanguard.edu Location: Employee Resource Center and Campus Safety Module (next to the Heath Academic Building) Why Work at VU Purpose-Driven Work Every role contributes to shaping students’ lives and advancing a mission centered on truth, virtue, and service. Growth and Development Focused Invest in your future with opportunities for professional growth and development and tuition benefits that support lifelong learning. Christ-Centered Community Work alongside colleagues who share a commitment to faith, collaboration, and caring for one another. Southern California Campus Enjoy a vibrant campus located in Costa Mesa, just minutes from the coast, offering a balance of meaningful work and an exceptional quality of life. Student Development gRADUATE aSSISTANTSHIP Opportunity Are you looking for a rewarding and practical means of applying your learning while pursuing your Master's degree? Consider a graduate assistantship under the Division of Student Development. click here to learn more Explore Our Benefits Your story matters here, and our benefits are designed to support you with health coverage, retirement, paid time off, tuition remission, and campus perks that help you grow and thrive. Explore our benefits footer-container-main Vanguard University A top private Christian university in Orange County, California 55 Fair Drive, Costa Mesa , CA 92626 Map & Directions Contact Us Facebook (opens in new window/tab) Instagram (opens in new window/tab) YouTube (opens in new window/tab) LinkedIn (opens in new window/tab) Schools & Centers College of Arts & Sciences Patty Arvielo School of Business & Management School of Education School of Theology & Ministry Global Center for Women & Justice (opens in new window/tab) Jesse Miranda Center for Hispanic Leadership Judkins Institute for Leadership Studies Lewis Wilson Institute for Pentecostal Studies Resources Job Openings Campus Safety Library Bookstore Registrar Events Press Room News Reporting Legal Notices Text Messaging Terms of Service Title IX Privacy Policy Reporting & Compliance Memberships & Affiliations footer-wrapper utilities Costa Mesa, CA Resources Site Map footer-tracking remarketing <div style=\"display:inline;\"> \n<img height=\"1\" width=\"1\" style=\"border-style:none;\" alt=\"\" src=\"//googleads.g.doubleclick.net/pagead/viewthroughconversion/1033647084/?value=0&amp;guid=ON&amp;script=0\"/> \n</div> footer-tracking sharpspring Powered by Finalsite"
